ven values:\n     \\[\n     |A \\cup B| = 40 + 30 - 10 = 60\n     \\]\n     So, 60 students like either apples or bananas.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of students who like either apples or bananas but not oranges:**\n   - First, find the number of students who like either apples or bananas but not oranges. This is given by:\n     \\[\n     |(A \\cup B) - O| = |A \\cup B| - |O|\n     \\]\n     Substituting the values:\n     \\[\n     |(A \\cup B) - O| = 60 - 20 = 40\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of students who like either apples or bananas but not oranges is 40.\n\n<answer>\nA\n</answer>",
