ce)\n   - \\( |M \\cap S| = 30 \\) (number of students who like both math and science)\n\n3. **Use the principle of inclusion and exclusion:**\n   The principle of inclusion and exclusion for two sets states:\n   \\[\n   |M \\cup S| = |M| + |S| - |M \\cap S|\n   \\]\n   Plugging in the given values:\n   \\[\n   |M \\cup S| = 60 + 50 - 30 = 80\n   \\]\n   So, 80 students like either math or science or both.\n\n4. **Calculate the number of students who like neither math nor science:**\n   - There are 100 students in total.\n   - The number of students who like either math or science or both is 80.\n   - Therefore, the number of students who like neither math nor science is:\n   \\[\n   100 - |M \\cup S| = 100 - 80 = 20\n   \\]\n\nThus, the number of students who like neither math nor science is 20.\n\n<answer>\nB) 20\n</answer>",
